"{tag1}W = 0.68:{tag2} Moderate agreement on adequacy rankings (r = 0.52 with "
"three raters)"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}W = 0.71:{tag2} Strong concordance indicates pathologists assess "
"severity consistently"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}W = 0.75:{tag2} Strong agreement - pathologists generally concur on "
"which cases are easy vs. challenging"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}W = 0.79:{tag2} Strong agreement on response ranking"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}W = 0.82:{tag2} Strong agreement (r = 0.78 with five raters) - "
"pathologists rank aggressiveness similarly"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}Weighted Kappa{tag2}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}Weighted kappa{tag2}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}Weighted Kappa{tag2} or {tag3}Gwet's AC2{tag4}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What each number is:{tag2} how far that resident's grades exceed "
"chance agreement with\n"
"                        one senior pathologist's grades on the same 100 "
"cases. It is agreement with a particular reader, not\n"
"                        a measure of diagnostic ability, and it absorbs any "
"error in the reference grades themselves - a\n"
"                        resident who is right where the senior reader is "
"wrong scores lower, not higher."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What Finn's coefficient reports:{tag2} the share of the score variance "
"that is not rater disagreement, on a case set where nearly every biopsy is "
"graded {tag3}none{tag4}. That describes how these four readers behaved on "
"these cases; it is not evidence that their grades are correct, since four "
"readers can agree on the same wrong grade"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What is computed:{tag2} (U - L){tag3}2{tag4} / (U + L) on 1 df, where "
"U and L\n"
"                        are the total counts above and below the diagonal of "
"the two-rater table\n"
"                        ({tag5}irr::rater.bias{tag6}). This is a "
"McNemar-style test of net direction."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}What is it?{tag2}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it does not tell you:{tag2} if instead B over-called G2 at A's "
"expense\n"
"                        and A over-called G3 at B's expense, the two "
"directions would cancel and this test\n"
"                        would return p = 1 even though the two pathologists "
"use the grades quite differently.\n"
"                        Enable the {tag3}Bhapkar{tag4} test for that "
"question. This test needs exactly\n"
"                        two raters; with three or more, compare them "
"pairwise or use the rater profile plots."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it reports:{tag2} the criterion is met or not met at the stated "
"limit and coverage; it does not by itself settle whether one measurement "
"method may take the place of the other in practice"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it shows:{tag2} The algorithm orders cases similarly to the "
"expert consensus grade; no outcome data enter the statistic, so it says "
"nothing about prognostic performance"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it shows:{tag2} The four pathologists order tumors by "
"aggressiveness consistently with one another. This is reproducibility, not "
"prognostic validity - no outcome data enter the statistic"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it shows:{tag2} The pathologists order cases by mitotic activity "
"similarly. Counts that differ by a constant factor still correlate "
"perfectly, so this is not agreement on the count that drives the grade, and "
"no outcome data enter it"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What it shows:{tag2} The pathologists order cases by proliferation "
"similarly. Correlation is unchanged by systematic scaling differences, so it "
"does not show that the reported percentages agree, and no outcome data enter "
"it"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What p = 0.001 shows:{tag2} the two criteria sets produce different "
"category totals on the same 90 biopsies by more than chance. The test "
"compares totals, not individual cases, so it does not report how many "
"biopsies changed category or in which direction any single one moved - the "
"contingency table in this analysis shows that"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What p = 0.03 says:{tag2} the algorithm's and the pathologist's "
"category totals differ by more than chance would explain. The test compares "
"totals only, so it does not say which of the two is closer to the truth on "
"any case - the pathologist's grades are the comparator here, not a verified "
"reference standard"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What p = 0.04 shows:{tag2} the reader's category totals moved between "
"the two readings by more than chance. A shift in totals is not by itself a "
"shift toward the correct diagnosis, and with a single uncontrolled "
"before-and-after reading the test cannot separate the workshop from practice "
"or recall of the cases"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What that does and does not show:{tag2} Marginal homogeneity is the "
"null hypothesis, so failing to reject it does not demonstrate equivalence. "
"The test also compares category totals only and is blind to case-level "
"disagreement, so pair it with a case-level agreement statistic and a "
"prespecified concordance margin before drawing any validation conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What the coefficient shows:{tag2} The three pathologists order cases "
"by fibrosis severity similarly. Rank correlation says nothing about whether "
"the assigned stages are correct, so it does not on its own support any "
"staging-driven decision"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What the numbers do and do not report:{tag2} the 3.2 mm is an average "
"difference over\n"
"                            200 cases and says nothing about how far a "
"single case can be off - the Bland-Altman limits of\n"
"                            agreement in this analysis carry that spread. "
"Because C{tag3}b{tag4} is not the only shortfall,\n"
"                            subtracting the average offset would leave the "
"two measurements still disagreeing."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What these ICCs cover:{tag2} how consistently each pathologist "
"reproduced their own\n"
"                            mitotic count across the two platforms, and how "
"consistently the four ranked the same cases, in\n"
"                            this one cohort. They carry no information about "
"the size of any glass-to-WSI offset, nor about\n"
"                            behavior at the mitotic-count thresholds that "
"change grade - the Bland-Altman output and\n"
"                            agreement measured at those thresholds are the "
"parts of this analysis that address those."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}What this analysis does:{tag2}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What this comparison can and cannot say:{tag2} it reports how "
"consistently the central\n"
"                            reviewers graded at two time points. It is an "
"uncontrolled before-and-after look with no group\n"
"                            that skipped recalibration, so even a real "
"difference could not be attributed to the\n"
"                            recalibration session rather than to case mix, "
"drift or practice."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What this shows:{tag2} the pathologist's category totals shifted "
"between the two readings by more than chance. With one reader, no comparison "
"group and no repeat reading without the workshop, the test cannot attribute "
"the shift to the workshop, and it does not say whether the new distribution "
"is the more accurate one"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What W shows:{tag2} The four pathologists order the biopsies by "
"inflammation severity consistently with one another. Concordance among "
"raters says nothing about whether their ranking matches the Nancy "
"Histological Index or predicts response to therapy - no outcome data enter "
"the statistic."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What W shows:{tag2} The four pathologists put the cases in a similar "
"order of difficulty. W measures concordance among rankings and nothing else "
"- no learning outcome enters it - so it does not establish that this "
"ordering picks out teachable cases or that a curriculum built on it works."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What W shows:{tag2} The pathologists rank aggressiveness consistently "
"with one another. It does not show that their ranking matches the FNCLCC "
"grade or predicts outcome - no outcome data enter the statistic, and "
"consistent raters can be consistently wrong."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}What W shows:{tag2} The six pathologists rank degree of response "
"consistently with one another; discordant cases are worth reviewing. "
"Reproducibility among raters is a prerequisite for, but not evidence of, "
"validity as a trial endpoint or predictive biomarker - that requires outcome "
"data, which do not enter W"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}When kappa is low{tag2} - the contingency table reveals "
"{tag3}where{tag4} disagreements occur"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}When PSA ≠ NSA:{tag2} the gap mainly reflects prevalence, not rater "
"bias."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}When to prefer them:{tag2} bootstrap intervals make no "
"normal-approximation\n"
"                    assumption, which helps for bounded, skewed statistics "
"such as a kappa near 1. They are not\n"
"                    automatically better than the analytical intervals: with "
"few cases or a rare category a resample\n"
"                    can miss a category, and the interval can be too narrow. "
"Read any dropped-resample note under the\n"
"                    table, and report which interval method you used (the CI "
"Method column says)."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}When to use:{tag2}"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Which statistic:{tag2} numeric columns holding only whole numbers no "
"greater than 10 are read as category codes and get kappa; a value with "
"decimals or above 10 makes the columns measurements and gets the ICC"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Why Finn:{tag2} ANOVA-based approach better captures improved "
"consistency than kappa"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}Why Finn:{tag2} Less susceptible to prevalence-related paradoxes"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Why Finn:{tag2} Provides meaningful agreement metric even with "
"category imbalance"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Why Finn:{tag2} Variance-based approach provides stable reliability "
"estimate in high-agreement scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Why Finn:{tag2} Variance-based model designed for low between-rater "
"variance situations"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Worked example:{tag2} four pathologists score Ki-67 (0 to 100%) on 60 "
"cases manually and with software that reads about 6 points lower.\n"
"                        Rater component 9.1, residual 3.2, between-case "
"variance 140: random share 0.26, so most of the disagreement is the offset "
"and a calibration factor is the first fix.\n"
"                        The same data with no offset but noisy reads would "
"show a rater component near 0 and a random share near 1."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"{tag1}Worked example:{tag2} two pathologists grade 80 carcinomas G1 to G3 "
"and disagree by one grade on 12 cases. A is typically around 0.85 to 0.90: "
"high, because most of the spread is between cases, not between raters. If "
"one pathologist graded every case one step higher, agreement on the values "
"would be poor (A drops sharply) although Spearman's correlation would still "
"be 1"
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid "{tag1}α {tag2} 0.667{tag3}"
msgstr ""

#: R/enhancedROC.b.R
msgid "{test} ({a} vs {b})"
msgstr "{test} ({a} ile {b})"

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid "{test} (J = {youden}, 95% CI {lower} to {upper})"
msgstr "{test} (J = {youden}, %95 GA {lower} ila {upper})"

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"{test} classifies worse than chance in this sample, beyond sampling "
"variation: Youden's J = {youden} (Agresti-Caffo 95% CI {lower} to {upper}) "
"on the {n} complete cases analyzed here. Its sensitivity and specificity add "
"up to less than 1, so calling its other level positive would do better; this "
"is the signature of a reversed positive level. Check the level chosen as "
"positive for {test} and for the reference standard before interpreting any "
"of these results."
msgstr ""
"{test} bu örneklemde, örnekleme değişkenliğinin ötesinde, şanstan daha kötü "
"sınıflandırıyor: burada analiz edilen {n} eksiksiz olguda Youden J = "
"{youden} (Agresti-Caffo %95 GA {lower} ila {upper}). Duyarlılık ve "
"özgüllüğünün toplamı 1'den küçüktür, dolayısıyla diğer düzeyini pozitif "
"saymak daha iyi sonuç verirdi; bu, ters çevrilmiş bir pozitif düzeyin "
"işaretidir. Bu sonuçlardan herhangi birini yorumlamadan önce {test} ve "
"referans standart için pozitif olarak seçilen düzeyi kontrol edin."

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid "{test} Has No Positive Results"
msgstr "{test} İçin Pozitif Sonuç Yok"

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid "{test} Has Only Positive Results"
msgstr "{test} İçin Yalnızca Pozitif Sonuç Var"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid "{test} in {stratum}"
msgstr "{test} ({stratum} alt grubu)"

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: {excluded} of {total} rows have observed results outside the "
"selected positive/negative pairs. Estimates are conditional on the selected "
"levels; exclusions are reported separately from missing results."
msgstr ""
"{test}: {total} satırın {excluded} tanesinde seçilen pozitif/negatif "
"çiftlerin dışında gözlenen sonuçlar var. Tahminler seçilen düzeylere "
"koşulludur; dışlamalar eksik sonuçlardan ayrı olarak raporlanır."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: {missing} of {total} rows lacked this test result or the reference "
"result and were excluded only from analyses requiring those values."
msgstr ""
"{test}: {total} satırın {missing} tanesinde bu test sonucu ya da referans "
"sonucu yoktu; bu satırlar yalnızca bu değerleri gerektiren analizlerden "
"çıkarıldı."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: {ratio} would be undefined because the cell in its denominator is "
"empty, so it was computed after adding {correction} to all four cells of the "
"2x2, giving {shown}. Every other statistic in the same row, including the "
"likelihood ratio that was not affected, uses the raw counts. Interpret the "
"corrected value cautiously."
msgstr ""
"{test}: paydasındaki hücre boş olduğu için {ratio} tanımsız olurdu; bu "
"nedenle 2x2 tablonun dört hücresinin hepsine {correction} eklendikten sonra "
"hesaplandı ve {shown} bulundu. Aynı satırdaki diğer tüm istatistikler, "
"etkilenmeyen olabilirlik oranı dahil, ham sayıları kullanır. Düzeltilmiş "
"değeri dikkatle yorumlayın."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: no false positive was observed, so LR+ is infinite, and adding 0.5 "
"to every cell would give a value of 1 or less, reversing its direction; LR+ "
"is left blank."
msgstr ""
"{test}: hiç yanlış pozitif gözlenmedi, bu nedenle LR+ sonsuzdur; her hücreye "
"0.5 eklemek 1 veya daha küçük bir değer vererek yönünü tersine çevirirdi; "
"LR+ boş bırakıldı."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: no true negative was observed, so LR- is infinite, and adding 0.5 to "
"every cell would give a value of 1 or less, reversing its direction; LR- is "
"left blank."
msgstr ""
"{test}: hiç gerçek negatif gözlenmedi, bu nedenle LR- sonsuzdur; her hücreye "
"0.5 eklemek 1 veya daha küçük bir değer vererek yönünü tersine çevirirdi; "
"LR- boş bırakıldı."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: PPA rests on {positives} comparator-positive cases and NPA on "
"{negatives} comparator-negative cases. A percentage computed on a "
"denominator this small is far less precise than the overall analyzed N "
"suggests. Enable the 95% CI option and read the interval before quoting "
"either figure."
msgstr ""
"{test}: PPA {positives} karşılaştırıcı-pozitif olguya, NPA ise {negatives} "
"karşılaştırıcı-negatif olguya dayanıyor. Bu kadar küçük bir paydadan "
"hesaplanan bir yüzde, analiz edilen toplam N'nin düşündürdüğünden çok daha "
"az kesindir. Bu değerlerden birini aktarmadan önce %95 GA seçeneğini açın ve "
"aralığı okuyun."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: PPA rests on {positives} comparator-positive cases and NPA on "
"{negatives} comparator-negative cases. A percentage computed on a "
"denominator this small is far less precise than the overall analyzed N "
"suggests. Read the 95% CI in the Agreement with comparator table before "
"quoting either figure."
msgstr ""
"{test}: PPA {positives} karşılaştırıcı-pozitif olguya, NPA ise {negatives} "
"karşılaştırıcı-negatif olguya dayanıyor. Bu kadar küçük bir paydadan "
"hesaplanan bir yüzde, analiz edilen toplam N'nin düşündürdüğünden çok daha "
"az kesindir. Bu değerlerden birini aktarmadan önce Karşılaştırıcı ile uyum "
"tablosundaki %95 GA'yı okuyun."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: sensitivity rests on {positives} reference-positive cases and "
"specificity on {negatives} reference-negative cases. A percentage computed "
"on a denominator this small is far less precise than the overall analyzed N "
"suggests. Enable the 95% CI option and read the interval before quoting "
"either figure."
msgstr ""
"{test}: duyarlılık {positives} referans-pozitif olguya, özgüllük ise "
"{negatives} referans-negatif olguya dayanıyor. Bu kadar küçük bir paydadan "
"hesaplanan bir yüzde, analiz edilen toplam N'nin düşündürdüğünden çok daha "
"az kesindir. Bu değerlerden birini aktarmadan önce %95 GA seçeneğini açın ve "
"aralığı okuyun."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: sensitivity rests on {positives} reference-positive cases and "
"specificity on {negatives} reference-negative cases. A percentage computed "
"on a denominator this small is far less precise than the overall analyzed N "
"suggests. Switch off the supplied prevalence and enable the 95% CI option to "
"read the interval before quoting either figure."
msgstr ""
"{test}: duyarlılık {positives} referans-pozitif olguya, özgüllük ise "
"{negatives} referans-negatif olguya dayanıyor. Bu kadar küçük bir paydadan "
"hesaplanan bir yüzde, analiz edilen toplam N'nin düşündürdüğünden çok daha "
"az kesindir. Bu değerlerden birini aktarmadan önce aralığı okumak için "
"girilen prevalansı kapatın ve %95 GA seçeneğini açın."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: the test was never negative in these cases, so LR- is 0/0 and is "
"left blank (its sensitivity is 1 and its specificity 0 here). A continuity "
"correction cannot create rule-out evidence for a test that made no negative "
"call."
msgstr ""
"{test}: test bu olgularda hiç negatif sonuç vermedi; bu nedenle LR- 0/0'dır "
"ve boş bırakıldı (burada duyarlılığı 1, özgüllüğü 0). Süreklilik düzeltmesi, "
"hiç negatif sonuç vermeyen bir test için dışlama kanıtı üretemez."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{test}: the test was never positive in these cases, so LR+ is 0/0 and is "
"left blank (its sensitivity is 0 and its specificity 1 here). A continuity "
"correction cannot create rule-in evidence for a test that made no positive "
"call."
msgstr ""
"{test}: test bu olgularda hiç pozitif sonuç vermedi; bu nedenle LR+ 0/0'dır "
"ve boş bırakıldı (burada duyarlılığı 0, özgüllüğü 1). Süreklilik düzeltmesi, "
"hiç pozitif sonuç vermeyen bir test için tanıyı doğrulama kanıtı üretemez."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{tests} diagnostic tests compared among {rows} selected rows. Per-test "
"available determinate denominators: {denominators}. Paired comparisons use "
"only rows determinate for both tests and the reference standard."
msgstr ""
"Seçilen {rows} satırda {tests} tanı testi karşılaştırıldı. Test başına "
"kullanılabilir belirli paydalar: {denominators}. Eşleştirilmiş "
"karşılaştırmalar yalnızca her iki test ve referans standart için belirli "
"sonucu olan satırları kullanır."

#: R/decisioncompare.b.R
msgid ""
"{tests} had identical observed balanced accuracy. {first} appears first only "
"because it was selected first; this descriptive tie is not a clinical "
"recommendation."
msgstr ""
"{tests} aynı gözlenen dengeli doğruluğa sahipti. {first} yalnızca önce "
"seçildiği için ilk sırada görünüyor; bu betimsel eşitlik bir klinik öneri "
"değildir."

#: R/nogoldstandard.b.R
msgid ""
"{unstable} of {starts} attempted starts failed, reached the iteration limit, "
"or returned an invalid likelihood ({failed} fitting failures; {nonconverged} "
"unfinished fits). The selected fit is the best converged solution when one "
"was available, but this pattern indicates an unstable likelihood surface. Do "
"not report the estimates without additional model checks."
msgstr ""
"Denenen {starts} başlangıçtan {unstable} tanesi başarısız oldu, yineleme "
"sınırına ulaştı veya geçersiz bir olabilirlik döndürdü ({failed} uyum "
"hatası; {nonconverged} tamamlanmamış uyum). Seçilen uyum, mevcut olduğunda "
"en iyi yakınsayan çözümdür, ancak bu patern kararsız bir olabilirlik "
"yüzeyine işaret eder. Ek model kontrolleri yapmadan tahminleri bildirmeyin."

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"{used} of {total} cases have both a test and a gold-standard value; any "
"further exclusions are listed below. Consider investigating patterns of "
"missingness."
msgstr ""
"{total} olgudan {used} tanesinde hem test hem de altın standart değeri "
"mevcuttur; varsa diğer hariç tutmalar aşağıda listelenmiştir. Eksiklik "
"örüntülerini araştırmayı düşünün."

#: R/decision.b.R
msgid ""
"{used} of {total} cases have both a test and a reference value; any further "
"exclusions are listed below. Consider investigating patterns of missingness."
msgstr ""
"{total} olgudan {used} tanesinde hem test hem de referans değeri var; diğer "
"dışlamalar aşağıda listelenmiştir. Eksik veri örüntülerini incelemeyi "
"düşünün."

