#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Kendall's coefficient of concordance (W) measures the {tag1}agreement among "
"multiple raters{tag2}\n"
"                        when ranking or rating ordinal data. W reaches "
"{tag3}1 at perfect agreement{tag4}, but raters\n"
"                        who agree no better than chance score about "
"{tag5}1/m{tag6} (m raters), not 0. The labels are\n"
"                        therefore read from the average Spearman correlation "
"between raters, which is 0 at chance\n"
"                        (it equals (mW - 1)/(m - 1) when there are no tied "
"grades)."
msgstr ""

