"                        context-dependent. A CCC does not establish that two "
"methods can be used in place of one another - that\n"
"                        requires a prespecified acceptable difference, "
"assessed with the Total Deviation Index or Bland-Altman limits."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Note: These cutoffs are adapted from Landis {tag1} Koch (1977), who put a "
"value exactly on a cut-point (0.20, 0.40, 0.60, 0.80) in the band below; "
"this analysis puts it in the band above. Different coefficient families "
"originate from distinct statistical traditions (e.g., Krippendorff 2004 for "
"Alpha, Cicchetti 1994 / Koo {tag2} Li 2016 for ICC) with different benchmark "
"thresholds."
msgstr ""

