#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Two pathologists classify 100 biopsies as benign/malignant. Results: 90 both "
"say benign,\n"
"                        5 both say malignant, 3 and 2 disagree. Observed "
"agreement = 95%, but kappa = 0.64\n"
"                        (“substantial”), well below what 95% agreement "
"suggests. The Prevalence Index = 0.85 (highly\n"
"                        imbalanced categories) is deflating kappa. PABAK = "
"0.90 (“almost perfect”)\n"
"                        better reflects the true agreement level."
msgstr ""

#: R/agreement.b.R
msgid ""
"Two pathologists read 100 biopsies for a rare subtype; each calls it in 2 "
"cases and they agree on 1,\n"
"                        so they agree on 98 of 100 cases. Cohen's kappa is "
"0.49 and Gwet's AC1 is 0.98. AC1's chance-agreement\n"
"                        term is less sensitive to prevalence, so it stays "
"close to the observed agreement when one category\n"
"                        dominates. Neither number is the true level of "
"agreement - they correct for chance in different ways -\n"
"                        so report the observed agreement beside whichever "
"coefficient was prespecified."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/cotest.menuSubtitle
#: cotest/options.menuSubtitle
msgid "Two tests run in parallel"
msgstr "Paralel yürütülen iki test"

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Two things that assumption-free estimation does not buy. Precision: the "
"sample is split across four or eight pattern cells instead of being pooled "
"into two marginal proportions, so the intervals are wider -- that width is "
"what the assumption was paying for. Transport: these numbers carry to "
"another population only if the whole joint distribution of results given "
"disease status carries over, which is a stronger requirement than each "
"test's sensitivity and specificity carrying over. Parallel and Serial "
"figures here will also generally NOT match the textbook independence "
"formulas computed by hand from the individual tests. With positively "
"correlated tests each strategy gains less than those formulas predict on the "
"measure it is chosen for -- Parallel raises sensitivity less, Serial raises "
"specificity less -- while the other measure loses less than predicted, so "
"Youden's J can be the same as the formulas give."
msgstr ""
"Varsayımsız tahminin kazandırmadığı iki şey. Kesinlik: örneklem iki marjinal "
"oranda birleştirilmek yerine dört veya sekiz patern hücresine bölünür, bu "
"nedenle aralıklar daha geniştir -- bu genişlik varsayımın bedelini ödediği "
"şeydir. Taşınabilirlik: bu sayılar yalnızca hastalık durumu verildiğinde tüm "
"ortak sonuç dağılımı aktarıldığında başka bir popülasyona aktarılır, bu da "
"her testin duyarlılık ve özgüllüğünün aktarılmasından daha güçlü bir "
"gereksinimdir. Buradaki Paralel ve Seri rakamlar genellikle bireysel "
"testlerden elle hesaplanan ders kitabı bağımsızlık formülleriyle "
"EŞLEŞMEYECEKTİR. Pozitif korelasyonlu testlerde her strateji, seçildiği "
"ölçütte bu formüllerin öngördüğünden daha az kazanç sağlar -- Paralel "
"duyarlılığı daha az, Seri özgüllüğü daha az artırır -- diğer ölçüt ise "
"öngörülenden daha az kaybeder; bu nedenle Youden J değeri formüllerin "
"verdiğiyle aynı olabilir."

